  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2003-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Write \\(\\overline{AMC10}=100\\cdot\\overline{AMC}+10\\) and \\(\\overline{AMC12}=100\\cdot\\overline{AMC}+12.\\)\n\nTheir sum is \\(200\\cdot\\overline{AMC}+22=123422,\\) so \\(\\overline{AMC}=617.\\)\n\nThen \\(A+M+C=6+1+7=14.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
